  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 60af0432a3c869e48a591344a8dafd71, type: 3}
  m_Name: PatDisc_4
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  question: "You\u2019ve been asked if you\u2019d be willing to donate a blood or
    tissue sample for research. You wonder what difference a small sample could really
    make. Later, a researcher explains how these samples are used early in clinical
    research to unlock critical insights about diseases and potential treatments.\nWhy
    might patient samples (like blood or tissue) be used this early in clinical research?"
  explanation: Patient samples are a powerful tool. They help researchers see how
    a disease actually behaves in the body, point toward promising targets for treatment,
    and even provide early clues about how people may respond to a new treatment.
    Without patient samples, researchers would be missing a crucial window into the
    real-world biology of disease.
  correctAnswer: 'D: All the above'
  incorrectAnswer1: 'A: To understand how diseases work in real people'
  incorrectAnswer2: 'B: To identify potential targets for treatment'
  incorrectAnswer3: 'C: To predict patient responses to treatment'
  questionRole: Patient
  questionType: MultipleChoice
  questionStage: Discovery
